      "description": "Numeric field with a visible scientific label and unit.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-field\">Maximum <span>dBZ</span><input type=\"number\" value=\"60\" aria-label=\"Maximum reflectivity in dBZ\"></label>",
      "css": ".ds-field{display:block;max-width:180px;font:500 12px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif;color:#586754}.ds-field>span{float:right;font-size:11px;font-weight:400;color:#5c6558}.ds-field input{display:block;width:100%;margin-top:8px;padding:9px 10px;min-height:36px;border:1px solid #dbe4d4;border-radius:4px;background:#fff;color:#46613f;font:12px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif;caret-color:#2b6b6d}.ds-field input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #7eb5b2;outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Workspace Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "navigation-selected",
      "description": "Primary workspace navigation with persistent selected state.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\" aria-label=\"Workspace navigation\"><button aria-current=\"page\">Radar workspace</button><button>Data library</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;max-width:210px;background:#f0f3ed;padding:13px}.ds-nav button{border:0;background:transparent;text-align:left;min-height:43px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:5px;font:12px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif;color:#5b6a5d;cursor:pointer}.ds-nav button:hover{background:#e6ede3;color:#284c40}.ds-nav button[aria-current=\"page\"]{background:#e0e9dd;color:#2d584a;font-weight:500}.ds-nav button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #257e87;outline-offset:5px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Provenance Badge",
      "kind": "chip",
      "description": "Informational label that distinguishes synthetic content.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-badge\">Synthetic data</span>",
      "css": ".ds-badge{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #dce6d1;background:#eef3e8;border-radius:3px;color:#5c6a51;font:11px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif;padding:4px 7px;white-space:nowrap}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Analysis Control Panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "control-panel",
      "description": "A flat bordered scientific control container.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2>Display settings</h2><p>Range and reflectivity bounds</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{max-width:260px;padding:20px 17px;border:1px solid #dfe6d9;background:#fbfcf9;border-radius:6px;color:#536852;font:12px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif}.ds-panel h2{font:500 13px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif;color:#476347;margin:0 0 20px}.ds-panel p{margin:0;font-size:11px;line-height:1.7}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Selected View Tabs",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Compact plot-view selection within a tonal track.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tabs\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Plot view\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">PPI view</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Regional context</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs{display:inline-flex;gap:4px;padding:3px;background:#f2f5ef;border-radius:4px}.ds-tabs button{border:0;background:transparent;padding:7px 10px;font:12px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif;color:#5c6556;border-radius:3px;cursor:pointer}.ds-tabs button[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:#fff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px #1f3c3014;color:#496840}.ds-tabs button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #257e87;outline-offset:5px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Send a Pulse",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "signal-button",
      "description": "The explicit trigger for the exhibition pulse.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-signal\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7.1 7.1a7 7 0 0 0 0 9.8m9.8-9.8a7 7 0 0 1 0 9.8M4.2 4.2a11 11 0 0 0 0 15.6m15.6-15.6a11 11 0 0 1 0 15.6\"/></svg>Send a pulse</button>",
      "css": ".ds-signal{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;border:1px solid #a8c4ba;background:#edf4ee;color:#456b60;padding:10px 13px;border-radius:5px;font:11px \"DM Sans\",sans-serif;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color .15s}.ds-signal:hover{background:#dcebe2}.ds-signal:active{background:#cbded2}.ds-signal:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #257e87;outline-offset:5px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-signal{transition:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Beam to Data",
    "overview": "A representative radar occupies a pale studio, with soft physical shadows, subdued metal and green-grey materials. Expressive large type and muted teal actions frame the instrument while an illustrative sampling field unfolds around it. The exhibition is spacious and spatial; the research workspace uses the same family of surfaces at a more compact, formal density.\n\nThe implemented system is a local research prototype. Representative models, illustrative echoes and synthetic datasets retain explicit labels. The analytical view keeps methods, units and provenance close to the output. Its visual confidence comes from clear structure and usable scientific controls.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Light studio material and cool sage surfaces.",
      "Expressive Manrope exhibition headings with DM Sans controls and explanatory text.",
      "Dark teal actions and a distinct scientific data palette.",
      "Thin borders, gently curved panels and restrained shadows.",
      "Intact physical instrument, rising sampled-gate field and a rendered static alternative."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Data Colour Rule",
        "body": "Preserve the ordered scientific palette for plotted values and their legends; interface actions remain in the teal and sage family.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Scientific Legibility Rule",
        "body": "Read the effective cascade through `src/legibility.css` and `src/exhibition.css` before reusing a size from the base stylesheet; the base stylesheet contains superseded small text values.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measured Depth Rule",
        "body": "Keep analysis panels flat and bordered; reserve cast shadows for spatial exhibition content and genuinely overlaid or selected controls.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the light studio and the formal scientific workspace as expressions of one visual family.",
      "**Do** keep scientific units, provenance and synthetic or representative labels visible beside the relevant material.",
      "**Do** use the effective legibility overrides when extending controls, legends and metadata.",
      "**Do** keep the rendered static poster for mobile and reduced-motion visitors.",
      "**Do** keep keyboard focus visible and use SVG line icons for interface controls."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** replace the pinned studio direction with an alternate visual world.",
      "**Don't** use the scientific data scale as decorative interface colour.",
      "**Don't** imply surveyed geography, a verified station model or measured data through unqualified visuals.",
      "**Don't** turn the landing's exhibition composition into a required layout for analytical screens.",
      "**Don't** inherit incidental small uppercase location, workspace or step labels as a general eyebrow pattern."
    ]
  }
}
